  "unitemized": [
   {
    "reason": "Applies only when no OpenSpec root exists (the two branches). Root absence is not expressible as a predicate, and the open-ended 'side effect' creation has no matching kind. The concrete 'openspec init' sub-rule is covered under ap-013.",
    "statement": "ap-012"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Conditional on the no-root branches, which can't be expressed as a predicate. Without that condition, writing under openspec/ is legitimate (for example, ticking tasks), so an unconditional prohibition would be wrong.",
    "statement": "ap-014"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Conditional on the root being absent, and no kind can tell whether a command created the openspec root as a side effect.",
    "statement": "ap-015"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Depends on the CLI returning state 'blocked'. CLI output state is not an observable predicate in the reference language.",
    "statement": "ap-023"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Depends on a blocked state with non-empty missingArtifacts in the CLI JSON, which is not expressible in applies_when.",
    "statement": "ap-024"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Depends on a blocked CLI state, which no predicate can observe, so 'implementation while blocked' can't be scoped.",
    "statement": "ap-026"
   },
   {
    "reason": "Depends on the CLI returning state 'all_done', which can't be expressed as an applies_when predicate. The verify stage document is read under the verify stage anyway.",
    "statement": "ap-027"
   }
  ]
